<!-- 
    Transmong Trader Entity Class Properties
    The following properties can be added to an entity class in entityclasses.xml to configure
    the behavior of the Transmong Trader's restocking system in the XUiC_WindowTransmongTrader.

    Available Properties:
    - RestockDays (integer, optional):
        Defines the number of in-game days between automatic restocks of the trader's offers.
        When the specified number of days has elapsed, the trader's offers (items and stock)
        are refreshed. If not specified, defaults to 3 days.
        - Minimum: 1 (restock every day).
        - Maximum: No strict limit, but large values (e.g., 100) delay restocking significantly.
        - Example: <property name="RestockDays" value="5"/> (restock every 5 days).

    - RestockHours (integer, optional):
        Defines the number of in-game hours between automatic restocks of the trader's offers.
        When the specified number of hours has elapsed, the trader's offers are refreshed.
        If not specified, defaults to 24 hours. Can be used alongside RestockDays, with restock
        occurring when either interval is met.
        - Minimum: 1 (restock every hour).
        - Maximum: No strict limit, but typically less than 24 for hourly restocks.
        - Example: <property name="RestockHours" value="12"/> (restock every 12 hours).

    Usage Notes:
    - Both properties are optional and can be used independently or together.
    - If both RestockDays and RestockHours are specified, restocking occurs when either condition
      is met (e.g., after 12 hours OR 5 days, whichever comes first).
    - Values must be positive integers. Non-integer or negative values are ignored, and defaults apply.
    - Restocking resets all trade offers, including sell items, currency items, and stock quantities,
      using the same logic as the reset button (calls RefreshOffers).

    Example Entity Class Configuration:
    <entity_class name="traderExample">
        <property name="RestockDays" value="5"/> (Restock every 5 days)
        <property name="RestockHours" value="12"/> (Restock every 12 hours)
        (Other properties)
    </entity_class>

    Example Scenarios:
    - Only RestockDays: <property name="RestockDays" value="3"/> 
        Trader restocks every 3 days (72 in-game hours), with no hourly checks.
    - Only RestockHours: <property name="RestockHours" value="6"/> 
        Trader restocks every 6 hours, regardless of day boundaries.
    - Both: <property name="RestockDays" value="7"/> <property name="RestockHours" value="24"/> 
        Trader restocks every 24 hours or every 7 days, whichever comes first.
-->